# BoardGames Meeting Planner — Project Context

A **React Native (Expo)** app for friend groups to coordinate meetings: vote on dates + games/options, approve a meeting, get push reminders. Multi-group with open self-signup. Display name **"VoteNMeet"** (rebranded from "Planszówki"). The app is a generic meeting planner, but keeps a first-class **board-games mode** (shared game library, meeting history/stats, win streaks) as a permanent special feature. Bundle id `com.jacaczap.boardgames`. Runs on **Android (primary), Web, iOS**.

## Tech Stack

- **Expo ~55** managed workflow + **expo-router** (file-based nav), React 19, RN 0.83
- **Supabase** — Auth, Postgres, Storage, Edge Functions (Deno), Realtime
- **gluestack-ui v2** + **nativewind** (Tailwind via `className`) for UI
- **TypeScript** strict, path alias `@/*` → repo root
- **i18n**: `i18next` + `react-i18next`, locales `en` / `pl`, device-detected, persisted in AsyncStorage (`lib/i18n/`)
- Web hosted on **Vercel**; native built/distributed via **EAS**

## Core Domain Concepts

- **Group**: the tenant. Every domain row (games, meetings) belongs to a group; all queries filter by the user's `currentGroupId`. Users join via a **per-group, multi-use invite link** (3-day expiry). **Roles** (`group_role`): `admin | approver | member`; creator = admin, admin implies approver. A user can belong to at most **3 free groups**; each group has a `member_limit` (free default 5).
- **Meeting**: the central entity. Lifecycle status: `voting` → `approved` → `completed`. Has a per-group `number` (unique on `(group_id, number)`). A "survey" is just a meeting in `voting` status.
- **Survey/voting**: users pick dates (`vote_dates`) and games (`vote_games`) in one `vote` per meeting. A vote with **no dates/games = "not participating"**.
- **Date options**: auto-generated **weekends + Polish public holidays** in range, plus user-added **custom dates**. Past dates are disabled.
- **3-play rule**: if a game has been played in 3 recent consecutive completed meetings, a new game must be picked (`get_consecutive_game_count`).
- **Approval**: **approvers/admins only** (RLS-gated by `can_approve()`, mirrored client-side by `useGroup().canApprove` / `roleCanApprove`) — pick date (sorted by votes), then game (filtered to that date's voters). Same roles can unapprove (→ back to `voting`); members vote but the UI hides approve/unapprove for them.
- **Late join** ("I will attend"): on an approved meeting, a user with no vote for the chosen date adds a vote for that date + chosen game.
- **Lifecycle automation** (pg_cron, daily): `create-survey` loops over groups, making a new survey 7+ days after that group's last completed meeting; `complete-meeting` marks past approved meetings completed → loop continues.

