## Data Model (Postgres, all RLS-enabled, membership-scoped)

- **groups**: `name`, `created_by`, `tier` (default `free`), `member_limit` (default 5). The tenant.
- **group_members**: `(group_id, user_id)` PK, `role` (`group_role`: `admin | approver | member`), `joined_at`.
- **group_invites**: per-group, multi-use `code`, `expires_at` (default now + 3 days), `created_by`.
- **profiles** (1:1 `auth.users`): `name`, `surname`, `avatar_url`, `notification_prior_meeting`, `notification_reminder_interval`. (No `username` — was dropped.) RLS: read own + profiles of users **sharing a group with me** (`shares_group`).
- **push_tokens**: `user_id` PK, `token`. Separate table so only owner reads it; Edge Functions read all via `service_role`.
- **push_token_events**: diagnostic log written via `log_push_token_event` RPC.
- **board_games**: `group_id`, `name`, `description`, `genre`, `min_players`, `max_players`, `tutorial_url`, `spotify_playlist_url`, `image_url`, `owners` (text[]).
- **meetings**: `group_id`, `number` (per-group, unique on `(group_id, number)`), `status`, `chosen_date`, `chosen_game_id`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `voting_start_date`.
- **date_options**: `meeting_id`, `date`, `is_custom`, `added_by`.
- **votes** (one per user per meeting) → **vote_dates** (`date_option_id`) + **vote_games** (`game_id`).
- **survey_reminder_log**: `(user_id, group_id)` PK, `sent_at` — per-user-per-group reminder throttling.
- **rate_limit_log**: server-only (no client access); backs `check_rate_limit()` for per-user insert throttling.
- **content_reports** / **user_blocks**: UGC moderation. Members report a game/profile/group (admins review under Group settings → Reports, resolve/dismiss); users block others (masks name/avatar app-wide via `UserAvatar` + `BlockProvider` in `lib/moderation.tsx`).

`board_games` / `meetings` carry `group_id`; `date_options` / `votes` / `vote_dates` / `vote_games` derive their group via `meeting_id`. Membership RLS uses `SECURITY DEFINER` helpers: `is_group_member`, `is_group_admin`, `can_approve`, `shares_group`, `is_group_member_of_meeting`, `is_group_member_of_vote`. **Abuse limits** are enforced by triggers (member/free-group/per-group/per-meeting caps + `check_rate_limit` on inserts).

Canonical TS types live in `lib/types.ts`. Key SQL functions: `create_next_survey(p_group_id)`, `create_group`, `join_group_by_code`, `preview_group_by_code`, `create_group_invite`, `get_consecutive_game_count()`, Polish-holidays computation (mirrored in `lib/holidays.ts`).

## Edge Functions (`supabase/functions/`)

Cron (daily): `create-survey`, `survey-reminder`, `meeting-reminder`, `complete-meeting` — all loop **per group**.
Trigger-based push: `notify-survey-created`, `notify-meeting-approved`, `notify-meeting-unapproved`, `notify-content-reported` (pushes new reports to group admins).
User-invoked: `delete-account` (GDPR self-service: verifies caller JWT, removes their avatar + deletes the auth user, cascading profile/memberships/votes). `verify_jwt` on (not in `config.toml`).
Shared push sender: `_shared/push.ts` (Expo Push API, batches of 100). Excluded from app tsconfig (Deno runtime).

## Conventions & Gotchas

- **Multi-tenancy**: every `meetings` / `board_games` query filters by `useGroup().currentGroupId` (`lib/groupContext.tsx`, persisted in AsyncStorage; switched via `GroupSwitcher`). Gate approve/unapprove UI behind `canApprove`. RLS is the real boundary — client filtering is just for correctness.
- **Realtime**: `meetings` + `votes` tables published; subscribe for live voter counts / approval changes. Use `useFocusEffect` to refetch on screen focus.
- **Storage**: private buckets `avatars`, `game-images`. Never store raw paths in UI — use `useSignedUrl` / `useSignedUrls` (`lib/storage.ts`, auto-refresh before 1h expiry). Delete old image on replace/delete to avoid orphans.
- **Alerts**: use `showAlert` from `lib/alert.ts` (cross-platform; web falls back to `window.alert/confirm`), not `Alert.alert` directly.
- **Strings**: all user-facing text via `t("…")`; add keys to BOTH `lib/i18n/en.ts` and `pl.ts`.
- **Web**: guard native-only features (`expo-calendar`, push) with `Platform.OS === "web"`. Web is centered max-width 700px.
- **Theme**: warm earthy palette — warm **brown** chrome (headers `#4a3228` / tabs `#3d2818`, border `#553720`, golden-cream text `#fef3c7`, cream bg `#f6f1e6`) + a warm **amber** interactive accent (default Tailwind amber: buttons/links `#b45309`, active tab `#f59e0b`, selected `#fbbf24`). Semantic roles centralized in `tailwind.config.js` (`theme.extend.colors`): `amber`(Tailwind default)=primary/interactive, `green`=success (`#5b7d34`, checkmarks/chosen/positive), `orange`=ochre warning, `red`(Tailwind default)=error/danger (vivid red for delete/danger zone, `#dc2626`/`#b91c1c`), `stone`=neutrals. Logo "n" is amber (`#f59e0b`). Note: the **app icon is the "VnM" tear-off calendar on a wood-grain background** (`assets/icon-wood-bg.png`) with a cream sticker contour; Android adaptive icon uses that wood image as `backgroundImage` (fallback `backgroundColor: #C89B6E`). The **splash** is the same calendar centered on cream `#f6f1e6` (configured via the `expo-splash-screen` plugin). Calendar art (`splash-icon.png`/`android-icon-foreground.png`) is transparent and kept inside the mask safe-zone so it isn't clipped. Utility classes keep those family names; inline hex in StyleSheets/nav mirror the same values.
- **Security**: anon key + RLS is the boundary (repo is public-safe). `service_role` only in Edge Functions. `.env` and `supabase/config.toml` gitignored.
- **Migrations**: never edit historical ones — add a new file. See `supabase-migrations.mdc` for required grants/RLS pattern.
- **Minimum supported version (force-update gate)**: implemented — remote `min_version` in the `app_config` table (Supabase, public read), checked on startup by `lib/version.ts`; outdated native builds are hard-blocked with an "Update required" screen (`components/UpdateRequiredScreen.tsx`, wired in `app/_layout.tsx`). Web is exempt; fails open on error. **Breaking-change rule**: for every change, check whether it breaks backward compatibility between backend and app (DB/RLS/schema/edge-function change, or removed client behavior). If it does: bump the app `version` in `app.config.ts` on the release that fixes it, and once that build is live raise `app_config.min_version` (via dashboard or a new migration) to lock out older clients. The two versions must move together (a shipped build's `version` must be ≥ the `min_version` you set). See `docs/version-gate.md`.
- **Git**: never commit/push without explicit user instruction; never to main/master.

> Note: `.cursor/plans/boardgames_meeting_planner_a7addda3.plan.md` gives origin design intent but predates the multi-tenant/groups rework (single-tenant, `username`, admin-created users). Trust the code/`lib/types.ts` when they disagree.

## Keeping This File Up To Date

When a change materially alters anything described above, update this rule in the same change. Triggers include: new/removed/renamed screen or route; new/changed DB table, column, or key SQL function; added/removed Edge Function or its trigger/schedule; new shared `lib/` utility or convention; stack/dependency or tooling shift; theme/palette change. Skip purely internal refactors that don't change the domain, data model, screens, or conventions.

